{Metaform_Schema} :=

METAFORM(
  id          := [metaform_id],
  description := [description of the AT and AUE present],

  elements := [

    # Each project element: the DE, and the SEs and NEs reached from it.
    ELEMENT(
      namespace_address := [code|document|media|data dotted namespace address],
      name_length       := [proper_noun_lookback_segment_count],
      name              := [Canonical Name (Project official terminology)],
      role              := [DE|SE|NE],
      purposes          := []
    ),

    # Each CQU: defined at downstream.cqu.
    ELEMENT(
      namespace_address := downstream.cqu.[CQU type],
      name_length       := [proper_noun_lookback_segment_count],
      name              := [industry title of the CQU role],
      role              := CQU,
      elements          := [],

      purposes := [
        PURPOSE(
          type    := purpose,
          purpose := [RE Operative Purpose],
          ef      := [PE Encounter Function within this RE encounter],
          ifd     := [send|receive|both],

          elements := [
            # The PE.
            ELEMENT(
              namespace_address := [dotted namespace address],
              name_length       := [proper_noun_lookback_segment_count],
              name              := [Canonical Name (Project official terminology)],
              role              := [DE|SE|NE],
              elements          := [],

              purposes := [
                # One level deeper: what this PE receives, in the same PURPOSE form, repeated at every depth.
                PURPOSE(...)
              ]
            )
          ]
        )
      ]
    )
  ]
)

# Notes
+> The element owning a purpose record is the RE; its nested element is the PE.
+> PE is not a role. An element may receive in one purpose record and provide in another.
+> purpose is the only purpose record type.
+> An annealed part is an element held by a purpose record one level deeper, in the purposes of the PE it is part of; it is not a separate top-level element.
+> An element is written in full where it first appears; where it appears again it carries namespace_address, name_length, name and role only.
+> Project elements remain under code|document|media|data regardless of join role.
+> upstream.* links external code|document|media|data that provide into the project.
+> downstream.cqu.* links external CQUs; other downstream.* entries link external receivers.
+> upstream/downstream are project-boundary links, not join-direction namespaces.
+> Links are not decomposed and hold no project elements beneath them.
+> An element's refs are items of the sources layer, not fields of the metaform.
+> Elements and purpose records nest in the same form at every depth. Trace as deep as the artifact's functionality goes; a part stops being traced on its own only where its parent's purpose carries it, never at the depth this template happens to show.
